    "%@ needs a one-time download from Apple. After that, everything you say stays on this phone." : {
      "comment" : "Language you speak: before a model download. The placeholder is a language name."
    },
    "%@ nights" : {
      "comment" : "Share card image (Body), drawn on a 1080px square and posted publicly. Headline, line 1 of 2: '12 nights / your body kept.' The placeholder is the number of nights with sleep data. About 18 characters. The number arrives as digits in a string placeholder, exactly as the English has always printed it (never grouped), so the catalog cannot vary it by count: phrase it so one form reads right for every count."
    },
    "%@ nights." : {
      "comment" : "Share card image (Milestone), drawn on a 1080px square and posted publicly. Headline under the seal; the placeholder is the number of nights spoken (2 or more). About 24 characters. The number arrives as digits in a string placeholder, exactly as the English has always printed it (never grouped), so the catalog cannot vary it by count: phrase it so one form reads right for every count.\nShare card image (Year One), drawn on a 1080px square and posted publicly. First headline line; the placeholder is the number of nights spoken. Display face, about 16 characters. The number arrives as digits in a string placeholder, exactly as the English has always printed it (never grouped), so the catalog cannot vary it by count: phrase it so one form reads right for every count."
    },
    "%@ sleep the night before" : {
      "comment" : "Entry detail, under the body-signal line: how long the user slept the night before this entry. The placeholder is hours and minutes such as '7h05'. About 35 characters."
    },
    "%@ stars." : {
      "comment" : "Share card image (My Sky), drawn on a 1080px square and posted publicly. First of two headline lines; the placeholder is the number of entries (stars). Display face, about 16 characters. The number arrives as digits in a string placeholder, exactly as the English has always printed it (never grouped), so the catalog cannot vary it by count: phrase it so one form reads right for every count."
    },
