    "%lldam" : {
      "comment" : "Stats > Your Week, Decoded: a morning hour, used in 'Happiest entries at <hour>.' The placeholder is the hour from 1 to 11 ('7am'). Use the local way of writing a time of day; 24-hour languages can write the hour as is.\nTwin tab > When You Write: a morning hour, inside 'Peak writing time: 9am'. The placeholder is the hour 1-11. A 24-hour language writes it as is (9 Uhr). About 6 characters."
    },
    "%lldh%@" : {
      "comment" : "Hours and minutes of sleep, as in '7h05'. First placeholder: whole hours. Second: minutes, always two digits. 'h' is the local abbreviation for hours. Keep it compact, about 6 characters.",
      "localizations" : {
