    "someone · %@ nights" : {
      "comment" : "Share card image (Year One), drawn on a 1080px square and posted publicly. Value for 'Brightest star' with names hidden: 'someone' stands in for the person; the placeholder is on how many nights. Gender-neutral. About 22 characters. The number arrives as digits in a string placeholder, exactly as the English has always printed it (never grouped), so the catalog cannot vary it by count: phrase it so one form reads right for every count."
    },
    "stays here." : {
      "comment" : "Share card image (Body), drawn on a 1080px square and posted publicly. Headline, line 2 of 2, when health data is off: 'Your body / stays here.' Display face, about 18 characters per line."
    },
    "this phone only" : {
      "comment" : "Share card image: row value meaning nothing left the phone, after 'Computed by' or 'Read by'. Lower case, about 18 characters."
    },
    "warm, steady" : {
      "comment" : "Twin tab summary: the tone part of 'Who you are: warm, steady, expansive.' Describes the user: keep it gender-neutral, lower case."
    },
    "%@ words" : {
      "comment" : "Stats > Your Week, Decoded: small stat chip on the insight card (also drawn into a shared image). About 20 characters. The number of different words used this week, as digits in a string placeholder (never grouped), so the catalog cannot vary it by count."
    },
    "Work" : {
      "comment" : "Life area (topic) of an entry: chip on a journal row and in entry detail's TOPICS row. One word, about 12 characters."
    },
    "%@x" : {
      "comment" : "Audio player: playback speed on the speed button, as in '1.5x'; the number is already formatted for the locale. Keep it very short.\nStats > Your Week, Decoded: a multiplier with one decimal ('1.8x'), already formatted for the locale, used inside 'You write <multiplier> more when you're <mood>.' Keep it very short."
    },
    "You asked %lld questions this week." : {
      "comment" : "Stats > Your Week, Decoded: insight card headline (large type, also drawn into a shared image). The card appears only for weeks the app could read, which today means English entries. The placeholder is the number of question marks in the week's entries (5 or more). About 40 characters."
    },
    "You haven't mentioned \"%@\" this week." : {
      "comment" : "Stats > Your Week, Decoded: insight card headline (large type, also drawn into a shared image). The card appears only for weeks the app could read, which today means English entries. The placeholder is a topic word from the user's past entries, shown in quotation marks. About 45 characters."
    },
    "You hit your weekly journaling goal of %lld entries. Keep it up!" : {
      "comment" : "Notification body when the user meets their weekly journaling goal. The placeholder is the goal, a number of entries per week (1 or more). About 70 characters."
    },
    "You know what you want. That's rare." : {
      "comment" : "Stats > Your Week, Decoded: insight card line under the headline (also drawn into a shared image). Under the 'want' versus 'should' headline. About 40 characters."
    },
    "You make sense of things more through…" : {
      "comment" : "Twin tab > 'How well does your Twin know you?' quiz: a question about the user, answered on a slider between two ends. Ends with an ellipsis: the slider labels complete it. About 40 characters."
    },
    "You mentioned %@ %lld times this week." : {
      "comment" : "Stats > Your Week, Decoded: insight card headline (large type, also drawn into a shared image). The card appears only for weeks the app could read, which today means English entries. First placeholder: a person's name from the journal. Second: how many times (3 or more). About 45 characters.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
