    },
    "You said \"should\" %lld times this week.\n\"Want\"? Only %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Stats > Your Week, Decoded: insight card headline (large type, also drawn into a shared image). The card appears only for weeks the app could read, which today means English entries. Two lines. 'should' and 'want' are the English words the user actually said (counted in English text), so keep them in English inside the quotation marks. First placeholder: count of obligation words (should, must, have to…), 5 or more. Second: count of desire words (want, wish, hope…). About 60 characters.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "You said \"should\" %1$lld times this week.\n\"Want\"? Only %2$lld."
